Ladybird resolves a replaced box’s intrinsic width
independently of the min-content contribution it makes to
its parent. Blink uses ComputeReplacedSizeInternal() for
the box and ComputeMinAndMaxContentContributionForReplaced()
for its contribution. Gecko resolves replaced sizes in
nsContainerFrame::ComputeSizeWithIntrinsicDimensions().
WebKit resolves the width keywords in
RenderReplaced::computeIntrinsicKeywordLogicalWidths().

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0 and WebKit 26.5 all preserved the
300 by 150 image under a 100% maximum in a 400px block, and reduced it
to 200 by 100 under a 50% maximum. A 20 by 30 canvas with a 60px height
measured 40px across in block, grid and flex containers. Chrome also
resolved a calc-size() adding 5px to min-content to 45px.

With a ratio-only SVG in a 400px container, Chrome and Firefox both
keep a 50px width under a min-content minimum. WebKit uses 300px. At
a definite height of 60px, all three use the 2:1 ratio and resolve the
minimum to 120px. Blink computes the keyword limits using the definite
block size or natural dimensions in ComputeReplacedSizeInternal().
